    "emails": null,
    "description": "**Position Overview**\n\nInoventures is seeking a qualified Neurologist to provide physician and medical officer expertise in support of CDC scientific and public\\-health programs. The physician will serve as a subject matter expert supporting the planning, development, implementation, analysis, and evaluation of scientific research, surveillance, and public\\-health activities. The position requires the ability to apply clinical neurological expertise within a broader scientific and public\\-health environment.\n\n**Key Responsibilities**\n\n\u00b7 Provide expert medical and neurological consultation to CDC programs and scientific initiatives.\n\n\u00b7 Support planning, development, implementation, and evaluation of scientific studies, research projects, surveillance activities, and public\\-health programs.\n\n\u00b7 Interpret clinical, epidemiological, surveillance, and research findings and translate evidence into actionable scientific or programmatic recommendations.\n\n\u00b7 Review research protocols, study methodologies, technical reports, manuscripts, presentations, guidance documents, and other scientific products.\n\n\u00b7 Assist with research questions, scientific objectives, study designs, analytical approaches, and evaluation strategies.\n\n\u00b7 Support epidemiological and surveillance activities involving neurological conditions or other relevant health outcomes.\n\n\u00b7 Participate in scientific working groups, technical meetings, advisory activities, and multidisciplinary project teams.\n\n\u00b7 Collaborate with epidemiologists, statisticians, laboratory scientists, toxicologists, environmental health scientists, researchers, and program officials.\n\n\u00b7 Support preparation and review of scientific publications, reports, presentations, recommendations, and other technical products.\n\n\u00b7 Serve as a technical liaison with healthcare professionals, researchers, public\\-health organizations, federal partners, and other stakeholders as required.\n\n**Required Qualifications**\n\n\u00b7 M.D. or D.O. degree from an accredited medical institution.\n\n\u00b7 Current professional qualifications, licensure, and credentials appropriate to practice as a physician and provide neurological expertise.\n\n\u00b7 Specialized education, training, and professional experience in Neurology.\n\n\u00b7 Demonstrated experience applying medical expertise to scientific research, clinical research, epidemiology, surveillance, public health, or related scientific activities.\n\n\u00b7 Ability to critically evaluate scientific and medical literature, research methodologies, data, and findings.\n\n\u00b7 Experience developing, reviewing, or contributing to scientific reports, manuscripts, protocols, guidance, presentations, or similar technical products.\n\n\u00b7 Strong written and oral communication skills and ability to communicate complex medical and scientific information to multidisciplinary audiences.\n\n**Preferred Qualifications**\n\n\u00b7 Experience supporting CDC, HHS, another federal health agency, or a related public\\-health organization.\n\n\u00b7 Experience with population\\-based research, epidemiological studies, disease surveillance, or public\\-health investigations.\n\n\u00b7 Experience supporting multidisciplinary federal scientific or public\\-health programs.\n\n\u00b7 Peer\\-reviewed publications or other evidence of scientific research experience.\n\nExperience translating clinical knowledge into public\\-health recommendations, research priorities, surveillance strategies, or programmatic decisions.\n\nPay: $92,340\\.62 \\- $111,205\\.91 per year\n\nWork Location: Remote",
